"## Summary\n\nAgent-core follow-up 51: r30's H-1, M-2 and M-3.\n- **Session:** launched 05:35 EST on 2026-11-04, and delivered at 06:21.\n- **Model:** codex `gpt-6-astra`.\n- **Size:** 5 commits and 12 owned files, +1,208/−12.\n  - The production change is +28/−11 in `node/agent`: `engine.go`, `sync.go`, `usage.go`, `observe.go` and `updaterecover.go`.\n  - The rest is the imported r30 proofs, the lane's own proofs, three test-only seams in the fake control server and the dated note.\n- **Checks:**\n  - merge-tree clean on current `main`; prepush-scan clean; owned-check passes.\n  - **The orchestrator reran these** on a scratch tree: `main` after #466 (`e39e7055`) with members 22 (#467), devstack 35, isolation 23, updater 26 and this branch merged in. All pass:\n    - `make -f mk/node.mk node-lint node-test node-test-integration node-build`, with the integration database;\n    - r30's six proofs in `node/agent` and `node/watchdog` by name, all passing. The agent file differs from the review branch only by the four removed TODO markers and the two recorded clock corrections; the watchdog file is identical;\n    - the R16 to r30, D-067, D-155 to D-157 and F48 to F50 proofs, over `node/agent`, `node/watchdog` and `node/enforce`;\n    - the lane's eight new tests by name, all passing;\n    - `go test ./node/updater/... ./node/nodelock/...`;\n    - `go vet -tags netlab ./tests/netlab/...`, so the lab compiles;\n    - `go test ./tests/handover/...` and the committed-evidence tests;\n    - `go vet ./...`, `make go-lint`, gofmt and `git diff --check`.\n- **Scope:** one ordinary lab in the lane's own prefix, with no rerun and no reservation. It waited 90 s for other lanes' runs first. An earlier validation attempt was held by host admission for about ten minutes and ran nothing. Zero owned Docker objects at the end.\n\n**The orchestrator's reading.**\n- **The diagnosis came first (D-141), on the unchanged base.**\n  - **H-1 is an engine API defect that neither CLI mode reaches.** `bootWithBudget` stored its caller as the engine's run context. A cancelled per-call `Boot` followed by a live `Step` could then skip recovery and admit forwarding, or keep `recovery_required` after the lock was free. A running recover child also died with the call's context. `fvpn-agent run` and `once` use one context for `Boot` and every `Step`, so neither reaches it.\n  - **M-2 is reachable in `run`.** A grant-less lease request is sent before desired sync, and sets the per-Step guard. If it fails, or gets an older generation's answer, the same Step can close recovery at the new generation, but the renewal finds the guard used. The lease gate stays at `policy_missing` until the next Step. This is a delay, not forwarding without a lease and not a permanent wedge.\n  - **M-2 in `once` mode:** only the older-generation-answer variant, after `Boot` retains a quarantine from a rejected restart adoption. The lane corrected its first diagnosis on this point.\n  - **M-3 is reachable** after a full 32-entry outbox, an unreported failure and a partial drain. A new closed recovery's clean report was then deduplicated against older pending items. It holds the early-renewal opportunity, not a forwarding permission. The lane reproduced it through ordinary Steps, not only through r30's direct construction.\n- **The changes.**\n  - **H-1:** only `Run` sets the run context now. Outside `Run`, no caller's context owns the recover child, and `Close` still cancels and joins it. Uploads keep exactly their previous parent, `Boot`'s caller, so cancellation still reaches their requests in both CLI modes. `recoverBlocked` is set before the stop check, and forwarding stays blocked until a configured recovery completes.\n  - **M-2:** each lease attempt records the ACK it sent. A held closed recovery may make one catch-up request for a newly available ACK, despite an earlier attempt in the same Step. The retry bound and Retry-After still hold, and recording the new ACK stops a second bypass for it. The accepted clean report then arms D-157's existing one-shot.\n  - **M-3:** dedup has one exception: a closed recovery that is waiting to bind its own report. The 32-entry capacity guard still comes first, and coalescing is unchanged in every other case.\n- **Unchanged:** D-155's exit-3 deferral, retry floor and fast wait; D-156's restart receipt; D-157's accepted report, one-shot consumption and Retry-After; D-067's cadence; D-135 and D-136. Forwarding still opens only on a populated lease and a verified Apply.\n- **r30's proofs.**\n  - **Imported byte-for-byte first** (`45cfee9a`). Against the unchanged code, all four addressed tests fail, and r30's two held-invariant suites pass. All pass after the fix.\n  - **Every assertion is kept.** The four TODO markers are removed, and the watchdog file is byte-identical.\n  - **Two manual-clock corrections, recorded in the note.** The rig's clock never advances by itself.\n    - H-1's second proof advances it by D-155's one-second retry floor before the second child attempt, so the floor stays.\n    - M-2's proof models one second elapsing during Apply, through a test-only plane wrapper. The fake control server's 503 carries the API's default `Retry-After: 1`, which syncLease correctly keeps. So in that case, a same-Step catch-up happens only if the second ends within the Step; otherwise the renewal waits for the next wake.\n- **The lab:** 13/13 on one attempt, 214.9 s.\n  - `TestLabD087_D104_GrantRenewalExpiryCorrelation`'s expiry phase: the last positive at D − 100.474 ms, and the first dropped probe sent at D − 63.778 ms. There were 97 positives and 15 drops.\n  - It is a functional gate, not an AT02 timing.\n- **No requests.** Members' next assembled AT02 run on `main` is the orchestrator's to schedule. Physical arm64 execution stays unmeasured.\n"
